Thread: #inc-2024-1112 — CSV export down for Halvorsen & Co
@dana: Customer Halvorsen & Co (single-tenant pod eu-3) can't run CSV exports — every attempt 502s. Started ~08:15 UTC.
@miguel: Found it — the eu-3 HAProxy backend route to the export worker was pointing at a decommissioned host after last night's fleet rotation.
@miguel: Route updated, workers recycled. Verified: ran 5 test exports as the customer, all completed.
@dana: Confirmed with the customer over email, exports working. Closing out. Total impact window: 08:15–09:47 UTC, one customer only.

Thread: #inc-2024-1119 — Load balancer config drift across fleet
@priya: Alert fired on config drift between HAProxy nodes; 6 of 8 nodes had divergent runtime state after an Ansible play partially failed.
@tom: No 5xx spike, no latency change, no customer reports — health checks were still passing on all backends.
@priya: Re-ran the playbook, all 8 nodes converged. Verified with config diff (empty) and synthetic checks. Marking resolved, zero user impact.
